CORE
array_write_variable_index_netlist1.sv
--aig --bound 2
^\[main\.p0\] .*: PROVED up to bound 2$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The netlist converter simplifies the elements of the array, which
rewrites an element of the array after the write as a conditional that
compares the index of the write with the index of the element. The
index of the element used to be of type integer, which the propositional
encoding does not support; it used free variables for the comparisons,
which refuted the property.
